<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Event Log Viewer (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/FormEventViewer`
    (FormEventViewer.cs + FormEventViewer.Designer.cs): a scrolling, read-only log/event
    viewer with a manual Refresh and an Exit button. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful
    re-platform of the currently rendered Windows Forms UI, never a redesign — every size,
    font and colour below is taken verbatim from FormEventViewer.Designer.cs.

    Window shell mirrors FormEventViewer.Designer.cs exactly:
      Text "Event Log Viewer"        -> Title.
      ClientSize 681 x 365           -> Width / Height (the WinForms client area; siblings with
                                        SystemDecorations="Full" likewise map ClientSize -> Width/Height).
      BackColor Gainsboro            -> Background="{DynamicResource AogLegacyGainsboroBrush}". This is
                                        the WinForms Color.Gainsboro (#FFDCDCDC) parity surface, centralized
                                        in App.axaml as the theme-INDEPENDENT AogLegacyGainsboroBrush (a
                                        sibling of the day/night ThemeDictionaries). Like the sibling utility
                                        dialogs (FormYesView / FormSavingView / FormInputDialogView) this
                                        colour is intentionally fixed for parity and does NOT follow the
                                        day/night Aog*Brush tokens. App.axaml's FluentTheme still supplies the
                                        default TextBox / Button control templates.
      FormBorderStyle.SizableToolWindow -> CanResize="True" (resizable, as the original) with
                                        SystemDecorations="Full" so the "Event Log Viewer" title shows.
                                        WinForms ControlBox=false hid the system buttons; Avalonia cannot
                                        hide only the close button while keeping a titled, resizable frame,
                                        so the standard frame is kept and the dialog's own Exit button is
                                        the primary close affordance (a minor, documented deviation).
      ShowInTaskbar = false          -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition.CenterParent     -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown owned over FormGPS).

    This is an IMPERATIVE dialog (parity with the WinForms code-behind), so there is intentionally
    NO x:DataType, no DataContext and no {Binding} — the partner code-behind addresses the named
    controls directly. The named controls below MUST stay rtbLogViewer / btnRefresh / btnExit to
    match the generated x:Name fields that FormEventViewerView.axaml.cs references.

    Code-behind contract — FormEventViewerView.axaml.cs (partial class AgOpenGPS.Views.FormEventViewerView : Window):
      * Parameterless / (string filename) constructor that calls InitializeComponent().
      * Owns the three named controls below: rtbLogViewer, btnRefresh, btnExit.
      * Click handlers (wired in this markup, following the established sibling convention where the
        code-behind defines the handler and relies on the XAML wiring):
            OnRefreshClick(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)  -> full reload   (WinForms btnRefresh_Click -> LoadLog()).
            OnExitClick(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)      -> Close()       (WinForms btnExit_Click -> Close()).
      * The WinForms File.ReadAllText / incremental tail-read + 1 s refresh Timer and the
        Log.sbEvents session append live in the code-behind, which writes them into rtbLogViewer.Text
        and scrolls to the bottom (WinForms AppendText / SelectionStart / ScrollToCaret).

    No WinForms, no OpenTK, no Win32 types are referenced — Avalonia 11.3 markup only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormEventViewerView"
        Title="Event Log Viewer"
        Width="681"
        Height="365"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogLegacyGainsboroBrush}"
        CanResize="True"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner">

    <!--
        Layout grid. Margin "12,12,12,4" reproduces the WinForms insets: the log starts at the
        designer's (12,12) origin with a 12px right margin, and the bottom command row sits 4px
        above the window bottom (buttons ended at y=361 in the 365-tall client). RowDefinitions
        "*,Auto" gives the log all remaining height and sizes the button row to its content (28px),
        matching the Top|Bottom|Left|Right anchored RichTextBox over the Bottom|Right anchored buttons.
    -->
    <Grid Margin="12,12,12,4"
          RowDefinitions="*,Auto">

        <!--
            rtbLogViewer — WinForms RichTextBox: Anchor Top|Bottom|Left|Right, Location (12,12),
            Size 657 x 315, ReadOnly=true, WordWrap=false, Courier New 14.25pt Bold. The 6px bottom
            margin is the designer's gap between the log's bottom edge (y=327) and the button row
            top (y=333). A read-only, multiline TextBox is the closest Avalonia parity to the WinForms
            RichTextBox log surface.
              * IsReadOnly="True"                 -> RichTextBox.ReadOnly = true.
              * AcceptsReturn="True"              -> multiline log (newlines preserved).
              * TextWrapping="NoWrap"             -> RichTextBox.WordWrap = false.
              * ScrollViewer.*ScrollBarVisibility="Auto" -> RichTextBox default ScrollBars=Both
                                                     (a horizontal and a vertical bar shown when needed).
              * FontFamily "Courier New", FontSize 19 (14.25pt x 96/72), FontWeight Bold.
              * Background White / Foreground Black reproduce the WinForms RichTextBox defaults
                (SystemColors.Window / WindowText) so the log stays a legible black-on-white surface
                regardless of the app's day/night theme variant (parity with the theme-independent
                Gainsboro shell).
              * AutomationProperties.Name labels the otherwise-unlabelled log region for screen readers
                (invisible accessibility — no visual impact).
        -->
        <TextBox x:Name="rtbLogViewer"
                 Grid.Row="0"
                 Margin="0,0,0,6"
                 IsReadOnly="True"
                 AcceptsReturn="True"
                 TextWrapping="NoWrap"
                 FontFamily="Courier New"
                 FontSize="19"
                 FontWeight="Bold"
                 Background="White"
                 Foreground="Black"
                 HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                 VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                 ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                 ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                 AutomationProperties.Name="Event log" />

        <!--
            Bottom command bar. Both WinForms buttons are anchored Bottom|Right; reproduced with a
            right-aligned horizontal StackPanel. Declaration order Refresh-then-Exit and Spacing="50"
            reproduce the designer's exact X positions over the 657px content width:
              btnRefresh : Location (261,333) -> right edge 440.
              btnExit    : Location (490,333) -> right edge 669 (12px from the window's right edge).
              gap btnRefresh.right(440) -> btnExit.left(490) == 50px.
            Both buttons are 179 x 28, Tahoma 12pt Bold (FontSize 16 == 12pt x 96/72). Standard Fluent
            text buttons reproduce the WinForms UseVisualStyleBackColor system-button look; the button
            text supplies each control's accessible name.
        -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="1"
                    Orientation="Horizontal"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                    VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                    Spacing="50">

            <!-- btnRefresh — WinForms btnRefresh_Click -> LoadLog() (full reload). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnRefresh"
                    Content="Refresh"
                    Width="179"
                    Height="28"
                    Padding="0"
                    FontFamily="Tahoma"
                    FontSize="16"
                    FontWeight="Bold"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    Click="OnRefreshClick" />

            <!-- btnExit — WinForms btnExit_Click -> Close(). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnExit"
                    Content="Exit"
                    Width="179"
                    Height="28"
                    Padding="0"
                    FontFamily="Tahoma"
                    FontSize="16"
                    FontWeight="Bold"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    Click="OnExitClick" />
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</Window>
